<small>To the chief Musician upon Jonath–elem–rechokim, Michtam of David, when the Philistines took him in Gath.</small><br /><sup><b>1</b></sup> Be merciful unto me, O God: for man would swallow me up; he fighting daily oppresseth me.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> Mine enemies would daily swallow <i>me</i> up: for <i>they be</i> many that fight against me, O thou most High.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> In God I will praise his word, in God I have put my trust; I will not fear what flesh can do unto me.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> Every day they wrest my words: all their thoughts <i>are</i> against me for evil.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> They gather themselves together, they hide themselves, they mark my steps, when they wait for my soul.<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> Shall they escape by iniquity? in <i>thine</i> anger cast down the people, O God.<br />
<sup><b>8</b></sup> Thou tellest my wanderings: put thou my tears into thy bottle: <i>are they</i> not in thy book?<br />
<sup><b>9</b></sup> When I cry <i>unto thee</i>, then shall mine enemies turn back: this I know; for God <i>is</i> for me.<br />
<sup><b>10</b></sup> In God will I praise <i>his</i> word: in the LORD will I praise <i>his</i> word.<br />
<sup><b>11</b></sup> In God have I put my trust: I will not be afraid what man can do unto me.<br />
<sup><b>12</b></sup> Thy vows <i>are</i> upon me, O God: I will render praises unto thee.<br />
<sup><b>13</b></sup> For thou hast delivered my soul from death: <i>wilt</i> not <i>thou deliver</i> my feet from falling, that I may walk before God in the light of the living? <br />
